    "sources": [
      {
        "what": "Owner 2026-10-16: XIM's own Black Ops 2 turn speeds (XIM game 4188, record types 150/151, plaintext): PlayStation hip 1013, aiming 264; Xbox hip 860.8, aiming 236.5; PS3 hip 846.8, aiming 224.5 deg/s. XIM lists no PC speed, so PC uses the PlayStation one. The dead zone, curve shape and up/down ratios below are our own measurement (D172), which read hip 2210, aiming 265.2 on PC (Plutonium, sensitivity Highest). The user curve on the owner's XIM for BO2 was the straight line."
      },
      {
        "what": "Measured on device 2026-10-01 by the ZeroStick Core's auto-calibration (D172), from 5822 of the capture card's frames: the scale from 3 full turn(s) (horizontal field of view 121.1 deg), every rate from a held stick's steady part, the fast ones timed by whole turns."
      },
      {
        "what": "Dead zone 0.075: between the still step at 0.070 and the moving one at 0.080, placed with the curve (power 1.83, worst miss 9.2 % of full)."
      },
      {
        "what": "Pitch 0.326 x yaw at equal deflection; aiming down sights 0.120 x hip. The turn climbs at about 4433 deg/s^2 from rest (accel), 31 ms from stick to screen."
      },
      {
        "what": "Seven full runs on 2026-10-01 agree: full stick 2198-2222 deg/s, a whole turn at 0.4 stick in 2045.6-2051.0 ms, every step from 0.20 to 1.0 within 1-5 %, aiming 257-267 deg/s. The dead zone's edge moved between runs (0.055-0.065 in four, 0.07-0.08 in three; under 0.15 stick the game turns under 15 deg/s either way). Raw data: docs/calibration/bo2-2026-10-01/."
      },
      {
        "what": "Replaces the sourced model of D164 (zone 0.20, 250/87 deg/s hip, 160/55 aiming, linear), kept in docs/calibration/bo2-sourced-model-d164.json."
      }
